-- title:
--   Ordinary adic Galois representation from a Hecke eigen-piece
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $N$ a positive integer and $S$ a set of natural numbers; let $\mathcal{O}'$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal and with finite residue field, with $p$ in its maximal ideal, and let $K$ be a fraction field of $\mathcal{O}'$. Let $M$ be a finite free $\mathcal{O}'$-module equipped with a monoid homomorphism $\rho_M$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$, realised as the $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphisms of `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, to $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal{O}'}(M)$, and with a ring homomorphism $T_M$ from the abstract Hecke algebra [`ModularCurve.HeckeAlg`](def/HeckeGalois_EichlerShimura.html#L14) $=\mathbb{Z}[X_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$ to $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal{O}'}(M)$; let $\chi$ be a ring homomorphism to $\mathcal{O}'$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_2(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$) and $U_q$ ($q$ prime, $q \mid N$, $q \notin S$). Assume: (hES) there is a two-dimensional $K$-subspace $W$ of $K \otimes_{\mathcal{O}'} M$, stable under all base-changed $\rho_M(\sigma)$, such that for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \notin S$ the base change of $T_M(X_\ell)$ acts on $W$ by the scalar $\chi(T_\ell)$, such that for every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $A$ and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition group of $A$ inducing $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field the trace of $\rho_M(\sigma)|_W$ is $\chi(T_\ell)$, and such that for every valuation subring $P$ with $p$ a non-unit of $P$ there is a one-dimensional $L \le W$ stable under the decomposition group of $P$ with $\rho_M(\sigma)w - w \in L$ for all $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup of $P$ and all $w \in W$; (hquad) for all such $\ell$, $A$ and Frobenius $\sigma$, the relation $\rho_M(\sigma)^2 - T_M(X_\ell)\rho_M(\sigma) + \ell = 0$ holds on all of $M$; (hunr) for every prime $q \nmid N$ with $q \neq p$ and every valuation subring over $q$, inertia acts trivially on $M$; (hcont) $\rho_M$ is adically continuous, i.e. for each $n$ there is a finite extension $L/\mathbb{Q}$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that every $\sigma$ fixing $L$ pointwise satisfies $\rho_M(\sigma)v - v \in \mathfrak{m}^n M$. Then there exists an adic Galois representation over $\mathcal{O}'$, that is a free $\mathcal{O}'$-module $V$ of rank $2$ with an adically continuous action $\rho$, such that for all primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ and every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $\ell$ for a valuation subring over $\ell$ the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2 - \chi(T_\ell)X + \ell$; inertia at every place above a prime $q \nmid N$ with $q \neq p$ acts trivially; and $\rho$ is ordinary at $p$, i.e. at each valuation subring $P$ over $p$ there is an $\mathcal{O}'$-submodule of $V$ spanned by the first member of some basis indexed by `Fin 2`, stable under the decomposition group of $P$, modulo which inertia at $P$ acts trivially.
--
--   This is the passage, in the style of Eichler–Shimura and of Wiles's construction of the ordinary $p$-adic representation attached to a weight-two eigenform, from a Hecke eigen-piece inside an integral Galois module with a decomposition-stable line at $p$ to a genuine rank-two representation over the coefficient ring with prescribed Frobenius characteristic polynomials, unramified outside $Np$ and ordinary at $p$. The ordinarity clause is obtained from the line in the base change to $K$ via [`GaloisRepAdic.isOrdinaryAt_of_stableLine_baseChange`](thm.html#GaloisRepAdic.isOrdinaryAt_of_stableLine_baseChange), and the result feeds the construction of the ordinary modular lift used in the modularity-lifting step.
